---
import policyStackConfig from "../../policystack"
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro"
---

<Base title="Privacy" description="How this blog handles storage, hosting, and analytics.">
	<div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-6 py-10">
		<h1 class="display text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight mb-6">Privacy</h1>
		<div class="serif space-y-5 text-foreground leading-relaxed">
			<p>
				{policyStackConfig.company.name} operates this blog and its self-hosted Umami analytics
				service. Analytics runs only after you allow it. If you decline or withdraw consent, core blog
				features continue to work.
			</p>

			<h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold">Analytics</h2>
			<p>With analytics consent, Umami processes:</p>
			<ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1">
				<li>Page views, URLs, referrers, and visit times.</li>
				<li>Browser, device, language, and screen information.</li>
				<li>IP-derived pseudonymous session and aggregate data.</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				Umami does not use cookies and does not track you across separate Umami website IDs. It
				processes the request IP address to derive session and aggregate values. The Umami script is
				removed when consent is withdrawn, and no form content is sent to Umami.
			</p>

			<h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold">Storage</h2>
			<p>
				Consent preferences use browser local storage. The blog theme uses a first-party browser
				cookie. These values stay on the current device and do not sync between devices.
			</p>

			<h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold">Cloudflare</h2>
			<p>
				Cloudflare hosts this blog and the future analytics tunnel. It processes limited technical
				request data, including IP addresses, for delivery and security.
			</p>

			<h2 class="display text-2xl font-bold">Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Send analytics or privacy questions to
				<a href={`mailto:${policyStackConfig.company.contact.email}`} class="acid-link">
					{policyStackConfig.company.contact.email}
				</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</div>
</Base>
